  "description": "NUPFIQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H56 Gd4 N12 O16,3(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.817-3.942 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.22-115.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(HL)4(CH3O)4]·3CH3OH (C75H67Gd4N12O20). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
